<Tunnel title="No Computer - Player Checks | Save My Gig!" status="Critical · No Laptop" red>
  <div class="review-flag">DRAFT, review pending.</div>
  <div class="step-label">Step 1 of 3</div>
  <h2 style="margin-bottom:1.25rem">Work the booth</h2>

  <p class="assumed">
    Taking it out, reseating it, trying the other slot and trying the other
    player are assumed done. These are the ones that get skipped.
  </p>

  <ul class="checklist">
    <li><strong>PRO DJ LINK.</strong> If the booth is linked, browse and load from a drive sitting in another player. Your dead drive stops mattering.</li>
    <li><strong>Give it thirty seconds.</strong> A large library mounts slowly and looks dead while it does. Most drives get pulled before they finish.</li>
    <li><strong>FOLDER view.</strong> If the drive appears but your playlists do not, the database died and the audio did not. Browse by folder and play.</li>
    <li><strong>Wipe the contacts, once.</strong> Worth ten seconds if you have not, not worth a third attempt.</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="tunnel-note" style="margin-top:0;margin-bottom:1.5rem">
    Older players can be fussy with very large or very new sticks. If you have a
    smaller, simpler drive with you, it is worth a try.
  </p>

  <p class="question">Does any player read it now?</p>

  <Choice step="no_laptop_1"
    a={{ href: '/saved?path=critical&branch=no_laptop', label: 'YES, IT IS READING', event: 'outcome_reached', data: { outcome: 'saved', path: 'critical' } }}
    b={{ href: '/protocol/critical/second-drive', label: 'NO, STILL NOTHING' }}
  />
</Tunnel>
